            </div>
            <!-- API DOCS -->
            <div class="panel" id="panel-docs">
                <div style="font-size:18px;color:var(--accent);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:6px">API Documentation</div>
                <div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--fg2);margin-bottom:16px">Static JSON API exposing every dump published on this site. No auth, no rate limit, CORS enabled &mdash; point any HTTP client at the files.</div>

                <div class="docs-note">
                    <b style="color:var(--fg)">Base URL</b> &mdash; in production, every path below is relative to the site root:
                    <code id="docs-base-url">https://deko661.github.io/hwidr-dump-site/api/manifest.json</code>. Locally, files are next to the page
                    (<code>site/local/api/</code>), so relative paths work over <code>file://</code> too.
                    <br><br>
                    <b style="color:var(--fg)">sdkContent.json</b> is split into parts to stay under hosting file-size limits:
                    fetch <code>api/sdkContent.json.part0</code> &hellip; <code>part4</code>, <code>JSON.parse</code> each part
                    (each is a valid <code>{"Category/Name": "header"}</code> object) and merge with <code>Object.assign</code>.
                </div>

                <div id="docs-endpoints"></div>

                <div style="margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:13px;color:var(--accent);font-weight:600">Examples</div>
                <div class="code-block" style="margin-bottom:12px">
                    <div class="header">JavaScript &mdash; fetch the offsets and read GWorld</div>
                    <pre>fetch('/api/offsets.json')
  .then(r =&gt; r.json())
  .then(data =&gt; {
    const gw = data.namespaces.Offsets.GWorld;   // "0x1b1d12f8"
    console.log('GWorld =', gw);
  });</pre>
                </div>
                <div class="code-block" style="margin-bottom:12px">
                    <div class="header">Python &mdash; load names and search</div>
                    <pre>import json, urllib.request

names = json.load(urllib.request.urlopen('&lt;BASE_URL&gt;/api/names.json'))
hits = [n for n in names if 'BP_' in n['name']]
print(len(hits), 'blueprint names')</pre>
                </div>
                <div class="code-block" style="margin-bottom:16px">
                    <div class="header">C++ &mdash; consume the offsets header directly</div>
                    <pre>// data.namespaces.Offsets maps 1:1 with the raw Offsets.hpp
#include &lt;cstdint&gt;

struct Offsets {
    uint32_t GWorld = 0x1b1d12f8; // from api/offsets.json
};</pre>
                </div>

                <div style="margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:13px;color:var(--accent);font-weight:600">Field reference &mdash; shapes returned by each endpoint</div>
                <div class="docs-note">
                    <b style="color:var(--fg)">names.json</b> &rarr; <code>[{"index": 0, "name": "None"}, ...]</code><br>
                    <b style="color:var(--fg)">objects.json</b> &rarr; <code>[{"index": 0, "type": "Class", "name": "/Script/Engine.Engine"}, ...]</code><br>
                    <b style="color:var(--fg)">typeCounts.json</b> &rarr; <code>{"Class": 12345, "Function": 6789, ...}</code><br>
                    <b style="color:var(--fg)">functions.json</b> &rarr; <code>{"ClassName": [{"name": "Foo", "flags": "exec=0x..."}, ...], ...}</code><br>
                    <b style="color:var(--fg)">offsets.json</b> &rarr; <code>{"namespaces": {"Offsets": {"GWorld": "0x..."}}, "rawOffsetsHpp": "..."}</code><br>
                    <b style="color:var(--fg)">decrypts.json</b> &rarr; <code>{"files": {"file.hpp": {"Namespace": [{"name": "X", "value": "0x...", "type": "uint32_t"}]}}, "rawHeaders": {...}}</code><br>
                    <b style="color:var(--fg)">sdk.json</b> &rarr; <code>{"Classes": ["AActor", ...], "Structs": [...], "Enums": [...]} <i>(names only)</i></code><br>
                    <b style="color:var(--fg)">sdkContent.json*</b> &rarr; <code>{"Classes/AActor": "// Class Engine.Actor ...", ...} <i>(split in 5 parts)</i></code><br>
                    <b style="color:var(--fg)">apex.json</b> &rarr; <code>{"mics": [[name, 0x..]...], "buttons": [...], "recvTables": {"table": [[field, 0x..]...]}, "convars": [...], "stats": {...}}</code>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- OFFSETS -->
            <div class="panel" id="panel-offsets">
